Redistribution or sublicensing must preserve the obligations in clauses 2 and 3.

3. Scientific citation condition
If the Software or a modified version is used in research and contributes to a
publicly disseminated scholarly output, the authors of that output must state
that Universal qPCR Analysis was used and cite its author, title and exact
version. This applies to articles, preprints, theses, dissertations, conference
papers, posters, scientific presentations and research reports, including use
of calculations, analyses, figures, tables or reports produced by the Software.
The citation must appear in the methods, references, acknowledgements or an
equivalent attribution section. Use a version-specific DOI where one exists;
otherwise use the software repository or archived release URL where available.
Absence of a DOI does not prevent use: author, title, year and version suffice.
For a modified version, also identify the modifications or derivative version.
CITATION.cff and CITATION_POLICY.md provide metadata and examples; they do not
waive this condition. Private research without a disseminated output does not
require a separate notice to the Licensor. Non-research use requires no academic
citation, but the notice-preservation condition continues to apply.

